{"_v":1,"id":"teeth-n-smiles-west-end-2026","cat":"west-end","cs":72,"rc":15,"bd":{"positive":6,"mixed":9,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Clive Davis","o":"The Times (UK)","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.thetimes.com/culture/theatre-dance/article/teeth-n-smiles-review-self-esteem-brings-jagged-drama-to-life-vrr7b0vz3","d":"2026-03-25","q":"The dialogue, though, is always jagged and intense."},{"cn":"Arifa Akbar","o":"The Guardian","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.theguardian.com/stage/2026/mar/26/teeth-n-smiles-review-theatre-duke-yorks-theatre-london-self-esteem","d":"2026-03-26","q":"Come for the play and stay for the astounding music."},{"cn":"Fiona Mountford","o":"The Telegraph","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.telegraph.co.uk/theatre/what-to-see/teeth-n-smiles-duke-of-yorks-review/","d":"2026-03-26","q":"Does it have anything of burning import to say to us in 2026? The awkward answer is a resounding 'No'"},{"cn":"Holly O'Mahony","o":"London Theatre","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.londontheatre.co.uk/reviews/teeth-n-smiles-review-duke-of-yorks-theatre","d":"2026-03-26","q":"But if this period piece is not exactly hard-hitting in 2026, it’s still a well-paced play running on a whip-smart script that’s very entertaining in all its salty sarcasm."},{"cn":"Alice Saville","o":"The Independent","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/theatre-dance/reviews/teeth-n-smiles-review-self-esteem-b2945628.html","d":"2026-03-26","q":"Daniel Raggett's staging makes the most of Hare's witty one-liners without sacrificing the essential bleakness of this story."},{"cn":"Tim Bano","o":"Financial Times","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.ft.com/content/2a3ee93e-f6fc-4196-b421-b8c68a010c97","d":"2026-03-26","q":"Maybe that’s to do with the gloss of the production."},{"cn":"Sam Marlowe","o":"The Stage","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.thestage.co.uk/reviews/teeth-n-smiles-review-duke-of-yorks-theatre-london-rebecca-lucy-taylor-self-esteem-david-hare","d":"2026-03-25","q":"Yet, the problems with Hare’s play persist."},{"cn":"Andrzej Lukowski","o":"Time Out London","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.timeout.com/london/news/review-teeth-n-smiles-starring-rebecca-lucy-taylor-at-the-duke-of-yorks-theatre-032626","d":"2026-03-26","q":"But as a complete production, it just doesn't work, and was probably never going to work."},{"cn":"Adam Bloodworth","o":"City A.M.","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://www.cityam.com/teeth-n-smiles-review-self-esteem-is-magnetic-in-dated-show/","d":"2026-03-11","q":"But ultimately too many of the narrative arcs, fights and breakdowns feel contrived and surface-level."},{"cn":"Unknown","o":"The Arts Desk","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://theartsdesk.com/theatre/teeth-n-smiles-duke-yorks-theatre-review-rebecca-lucy-taylor-smash","d":"2026-03-25","q":"His verdict: “thoroughly entertaining”, and sure to “enjoy a long and sold-out run at the beautiful Savoy Theatre.”"},{"cn":"Unknown","o":"London Box Office","s":84,"b":"Rave","t":3,"d":"2026-03-25"},{"cn":"Alexander Cohen","o":"BroadwayWorld","s":63,"b":"Mixed","t":3,"u":"https://www.broadwayworld.com/westend/article/TEETH-N-SMILES-Duke-Of-Yorks-20260326","d":"2026-03-26","q":"There's fun to be had in Daniel Raggett's production, stripping away distraction and funnelling all attention onto Maggie's slow-motion implosion."},{"cn":"The Reviews Hub - London","o":"The Reviews Hub","s":61,"b":"Mixed","t":3,"u":"https://www.thereviewshub.com/teeth-n-smiles-duke-of-yorks-theatre-london/","d":"2026-03-26","q":"What they seem unable to provide, however, is the energy, the power, the flash of a good rock band."},{"cn":"Unknown","o":"Musical Theatre Review","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":3,"u":"https://musicaltheatrereview.com/teeth-n-smiles-duke-of-yorks-theatre/","d":"2026-03-25","q":"Beyond that, this David Hare revival is toothless."},{"cn":"Greg Stewart","o":"Theatre Weekly","s":60,